text:
marco: Quick UX tradeoff question: do we optimize the trace detail for button density (lots of small icon actions) or for discoverability (fewer visible actions + explicit labels)? Figma: https://www.figma.com/file/zzzz

rina: My vote is discoverability. New users keep missing the copy/permalink. Icon-only saves space but increases support noise.

devon: Agree on discoverability for detail pages. For list rows, density is okay because users are scanning many items. We should design two responsive variants: dense list vs descriptive detail.

sam: Accessibility checklist: any icon-only affordance must have aria-label and tooltip. Also ensure focus order is logical: Title -> Meta -> Primary actions -> Secondary menu. If we hide labels visually, expose full text to screen readers.

marco: Concrete pattern proposal: show full labeled buttons on detail (Copy correlation ID, Share permalink, Download) and compress to icon + tooltip in list. Add a persistent kebab for less-frequent actions. Thoughts?

rina: Works. One nuance: when we compress to icon-only in lists, show a subtle chevron or affordance on hover/focus to avoid invisible targets. Also make the copy icon larger hit target (44px).

devon: Instrumentation: track `trace_ui_action` events with props: action (copy_id|copy_permalink|download), ui_variant (detail|list|bulk), result (success|fail). Don't log full ids; include masked_id or last6.

sam: Keyboard flows: for list rows, make the copy icon reachable via Tab in each row (not by arrow navigation only). For dense tables we should also support row-level keyboard commands (e.g., press 'c' when row is focused to copy). Provide an assistive hint for that (only shown once).

marco: UX question: toast wording. Short: "Correlation ID copied" vs more descriptive: "Correlation ID copied to clipboard". Which is better for SRs?

sam: Use the longer phrase for SRs and aria-live. For visual toast we can display the short text and include the aria-live element with the full sentence so SRs hear the explicit copy target. Example: <code>&lt;div role:\"status\" aria-live:\"polite\"&gt;Correlation ID copied to clipboard&lt;/div&gt;</code>

rina: Also add a visible undo or "Show ID" action in the toast when clipboard fails: "Copy failed. Show full ID" which selects the text for manual copying. Keep messages actionable.

devon: Implementation snippet suggestion for masked analytics and clipboard fallback:

<code>
async function copyCorrId(id) {
  try {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(id);
    analytics.track('trace_ui_action', { action: 'copy_id', ui_variant, result: 'success', masked_id: id.slice(-6) });
    announce('Correlation ID copied to clipboard');
  } catch (err) {
    analytics.track('trace_ui_action', { action: 'copy_id', ui_variant, result: 'fail', error: err.code });
    showFallbackSelect(id);
  }
}
</code>

marco: Nice. Another tiny UI decision: should the copy button show the full ID on hover in a tooltip? That leaks long ids into hovercard which could be noisy. Maybe show only on detail page, not list.

sam: Agreed. Tooltip with full ID only in detail. For lists use aria-label to expose full value to SRs but not show it visually. Also ensure truncation uses an accessible title attribute as last resort.

rina: Mobile: use a long-press menu on the corr-id to expose copy + share, since tooltips don't work. Make sure long-press is discoverable via an inline hint the first time.

devon: Bulk export: when users select >1 trace, surface a sticky bar with primary actions (Download JSON) and a kebab for format choices. Keep analytics prop `selected_count` in the event.

marco: Anything else for accessibility?

sam: Ensure color contrast for labels and icons (4.5:1 for text). Provide visible focus states for every interactive control. Use role=menu & role=menuitem for kebab menus; trap focus in modal menus and restore focus after close. Test with NVDA/VoiceOver/TalkBack.

a11y-bot: Created tickets: D-6101 (Detail labeled actions), D-6102 (List icon-only pattern + focus targets), D-6103 (Clipboard fallback & toasts), D-6104 (Mobile long-press menu) :rocket:

marco: Action items: 1) I'll update Figma with labeled detail buttons + dense list icons by Tue EOD. 2) devon please draft the analytics spec with masked ids by Wed. 3) sam add keyboard shortcuts & aria-live examples to the component doc by Wed. 4) rina write the mobile long-press spec by Thu.

rina: I'll also mock the first-run hint for keyboard row commands.

marco: Great. Closing thread; I'll link updated mocks. Thanks!
